1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,028
Day 59: Heretic, a tool that removes a model's refusals

2
00:00:04,028 --> 00:00:05,420
without retraining.

3
00:00:05,420 --> 00:00:07,984
Its quality score said zero damage.

4
00:00:07,984 --> 00:00:09,961
It wasn't measuring damage.

5
00:00:10,411 --> 00:00:12,913
Heretic edits a model to stop refusing,

6
00:00:12,913 --> 00:00:16,762
and uses KL divergence from the original model to check that

7
00:00:16,762 --> 00:00:17,981
nothing else broke.

8
00:00:18,431 --> 00:00:22,013
Each Optuna trial removes the refusal direction with different

9
00:00:22,013 --> 00:00:23,168
strength and layers.

10
00:00:23,618 --> 00:00:25,142
Then it scores refusals,

11
00:00:25,142 --> 00:00:28,761
and KL divergence on just the first token of each answer.

12
00:00:29,211 --> 00:00:31,870
Qwen3 always starts with a think tag.

13
00:00:31,870 --> 00:00:36,038
Heretic normally skips it, but our config turned that off.

14
00:00:36,488 --> 00:00:39,791
So KL stayed near zero in almost every trial.

15
00:00:39,791 --> 00:00:41,552
With the prefix back on,

16
00:00:41,552 --> 00:00:44,341
KL rose about two hundred forty times.

17
00:00:44,341 --> 00:00:48,524
On the 4B model, every zero-refusal trial came with heavy

18
00:00:48,524 --> 00:00:49,038
damage.

19
00:00:49,488 --> 00:00:52,314
Only aggregate scores were recorded.

20
00:00:52,314 --> 00:00:55,140
Full numbers are on Zenn and GitHub.

21
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:56,710
Heretic is AGPL-3.0.
